hi everyone its Johanna here I thought I  would take the time and share something  quite personal which I had struggled  with for over 2 to 3 years and that was  acne most of you might not know this but  I had pretty bad  acne from the end of 2009 till about  2012 so I wasn't blessed with natural  glowy skin or clear skin before I start  I just want to be clear that I am NOT a  skin expert in fact I have a very  limited knowledge in skincare and makeup  so what I'm sharing with you today is  based on my own personal experience and  what has worked for me what you're  looking at right now it's me without any  cream or foundation on just a little bit  of eye makeup because if I don't put any  eye makeup you will not be able to see  my eyes they're so small so as you can  see there's still a little bit of scar  and redness from my acne growing up as a  teenager I never had acne it first  started during my final year of college  and we came back right now it was really  done to poor nutrition lack of exercise  lack of sleep and high amount of stress  which messed up my hormones back in 2009  I was juggling b2 my college work  full-time internship and I also started  my part-time personal training course  over the weekends and what many was was  when I left home for college I did not  enjoy any more home-cooked meals and I  did not have a clue on how to make my  own meals so I was constantly eating out  every day on every single meals I did  not care what goes into my mouth how big  the portion was at what time of the day  so I was staying up really late at night  and I was eating a big greasy meal at 3  or 4 a.m. in the morning and I only had  about 3 or 4 hours of sleep a day so  this picture you're looking at right now  was taken towards the end of 2  that night when I first started  developing acne after a year of really  poor life style when I started  developing acne the first reaction was  to get stress and to get panic so I  decided to take things into my own hands  bearing in mind that I had very little  knowledge on skincare and nutrition at  that time every time I stand to the  mirror I would be really upset and my  hands would be touching my face trying  to pop and acne out instead of doing my  usual cleansing or to have a better diet  and lifestyle I ended up scrubbing my  face every day my thought was that the  more I scrub eventually all the acne  will pop out and disappear and of course  that did not happen and as you know it  only made my skin worse so I decided to  go to the pharmacies and get some  medications I start to apply the  medication and I guess what I was  looking for was a miracle cream I was  hoping that by applying the medication  for a week and it would just go off I  even did my own online research trying  to look for a miracle cream just like  some of you who might be looking for a  quick fix on weight loss  I bought the cream and of course nothing  worked eventually I ended up going to a  dermatologist and to be honest it wasn't  a really positive experience for me in  his opinion my skin condition was  nothing in comparison to his other  patients so all he did was to stare at  my face for about 30 seconds and I'm not  even kidding  give me some medications and cream to  apply and off I go so I did apply the  cream and took the medications for the  next six months and it did help to  improve my acne but once I stopped it  came back again and it's because I did  not get down to the core of the problem  which was my really poor lifestyle bad  nutrition lack of exercise and just  constant stress and lack of sleep all  these events happen in a cost of just  over a year and at a time I really  really hate to looking at myself in the  mirror it's because before my acne I  used to do  part-time modeling and acting and once I  had my acne I wasn't able to do any of  that anymore and so looking at myself  every day in the mirror just made myself  hated the way I look  eventually I got fed up and just give up  on treatments and really not caring  about myself anymore  and unknowingly at that time I started  looking more into my own nutrition  exercise and sleeping habits as I  started working as a personal trainer so  I started exercising on a regular basis  care more about my food slap at least  eight hours per night and this helped to  reduce my stress level all of this did  not happen overnight  in fact it happened over two years of  ups and downs and eventually when I came  to the UK towards in the end of 2010 my  skin started to break out again because  I wasn't used to the weather here it was  too dry for me adjusting to the food  here was another challenge for me so  being so far away from home and not  having much I had to start prepping my  own meals with very limited knowledge I  prep really basic meals which I believe  actually helped me towards curing my  acne and what was really important for  me was when I learned to put my physical  appearance aside to be able to look into  the mirror and to be truly happy with  who I am despite having a lot of acne  slowly as my frustration and stress went  away day by day I had clearer and  clearer skin so let me share with you 10  tips that has worked for me let me start  with nutrition the first tip is to eat  basic real food as much as you can try  to prep your own meals eating out too  often and not knowing what goes into my  food was one of the causes to my acne  what I mean by basic real food is to  choose whole food minimal ingredients  which doesn't require much time to prep  at all so my food recipes videos are  basically the type of food I have been  consuming for the past two years which  has helped towards my acne  it has helped towards my weight  maintenance as well the second tip is to  cut down on greasy food consuming greasy  food really messes with my digestion and  it makes me feel as though my pores are  opening up and it gives me early skin I  know there are no proven science behind  this but this is based on my own  personal experience and cutting down on  greasy food has helped me to gain  clearer skin this then leads on to my  next point which is to consume more food  that helps with better digestion when I  had my acne I had a really poor  digestion not only did I feel bloated  almost every day poor digestion has  caused my skin pores to clock so foods  that help with digestion are basically  foods which are high in fiber and water  content such as vegetables and fruits my  all-time favorite is banana food that  you should avoid are greasy fried oily  food and dairy products if you are  lactose intolerance the fourth tip is to  be aware of your sodium intake this is  true in my case when I used to eat out  every single day the meals I used to  consume were either processed food fast  food or meals which are high in sodium  not only if these meals made me feel so  bloated but they also managed to ruin my  skin so again it comes down to the  principle of preparing your own meals  it's in clean unprocessed food which are  low in sodium this has made me feel  better  and to give me clearer skin as well tip  number 5 is to drink more water as  obvious as this might sound sometimes  with our busy schedule especially during  my stressful period we tend to forget to  keep ourselves hydrated at all time  drinking more water helps to flush our  internal toxins which has helped to  reduce my break out tremendously and  drinking more water has also kept my  skin hydrated inside out and this was  needed when I first came to the UK and  when I was still adjusting to the dry  weather here  Plus drinking water helps to keep you  young helps to keep the weight off and  to stay fit  so keep drinking and drinking another  method I use to get more fluid into my  body is to consume food with high water  content when I was in Malaysia I used to  drink a lot of coconut water and  watermelon juice are the foods with high  water content include strawberries  zucchinis cucumbers spinach tomatoes  broccolis and more what you can do is to  boil and blend your favorite vegetables  to make a thick and creamy vegetable  soup which is currently my favorite dish  the next tip is to cleanse twice a day  again this is my son really obvious but  when I was awake at 3 or 4 a.m. in the  morning I wasn't thinking about  cleansing my face so just like getting  into a fitness routine I had to get  myself into a cleansing routine to  cleanse in the morning and at night and  to trust that all these changes I'm  making every day will help towards my  skin remember my acne did not go away  overnight it was 2 to 3 years of ups and  downs for me so just like losing weight  you have to start making the changes and  to trust that all these positive changes  you're making will help towards your  results for those of you who do your  regular exercises threat from exercising  can also lead to breakouts by your skin  irritation especially around your  forehead so it is very important for you  to cleanse and shower right after your  workouts and to wear fresh clothes do  not wait for hours to shower shower once  you have cooled down tip number 8 is do  not skip on your beauty sleep lack of  sleep increases stress and stress leads  to breakup and weight gain I personally  experienced both of this in my final  year of college when I finally get my  life back into more of an order  naturally my skin starts to appear  as well so even up to today if I like my  beauty sleep I can see and feel the  difference on my skin sleep for at least  seven to eight hours every day the next  tip is to exercise regularly exercising  has so many more health benefits  including clear skin exercising on a  regular basis has helped me to reduce my  stress level and to regulate my hormone  levels which is one of the main causes  of acne so if you want clearer skin  filter body better health and to look  good and feel good inside out do your  regular exercises my final and most  important tip is focus on the change and  not the problem this is true whether  you're struggling with acne or to lose  weight or any other life circumstances  focusing on the problem will not make  the problem go away instead focus your  energy into making the changes which  will eventually solve the problem I had  to learn this the hard way my acne will  not go away in fact it only was done  with the stress and self-hatred my skin  only became clearer when I started to  love myself again to focus on the  positive changes I made daily and to  slowly reboot my confidence by putting  my physical appearance aside hence I  always believe that we have to learn to  love ourselves as who we are right now  before any changes can happen just like  being consistent with your workout and  meal plan to lose weight I had to be  consistent with my skincare routine in  order for my acne to heal once you have  set your mind to a goal my being to cure  my acne you have to stop having doubts  and start having faith that every  positive changes you make will only lead  you towards your goal no matter how long  it will take you stick by it  it took me two years to have clear skin  but this has helped me to regain my  confidence and for me to love myself  even more so start having faith for new  fitness food and motivational videos  please like share and subscribe to my  youtube channel and website do follow me  on Facebook Instagram and Twitter to  stay connected with me thanks guys
 

